51. Bus Passenger Occupancy Simulation
1. Problem Statement
Process passenger boarding and alighting counts at several bus stops, calculate occupancy after every stop, and flag
capacity violations.
2. Objectives
Track passengers stop by stop; prevent negative passenger counts; identify when bus capacity is exceeded.
3. Assumptions
The bus starts empty. At each stop, alighting passengers leave before new passengers board. Bus capacity is 40. Inputs
are non-negative integers and alighting cannot exceed current occupancy.
4. Algorithm
• Set capacity and current passengers to 40 and 0.
• For each stop, read alighting and boarding counts.
• If alighting exceeds current passengers, report invalid data. Otherwise subtract alighting and add boarding.
• Display occupancy and flag any value above capacity.
5. Flowchart
Start → Set capacity and occupancy → Read alighting/boarding at each stop → Validate counts → Update occupancy →
Check capacity → Display result → More stops? (yes: repeat; no: End)
6. Pseudocode
START\ncapacity ← 40; passengers ← 0\nFOR each stop\n INPUT alighting, boarding\n IF alighting > passengers OR counts are ne
7. Python Source Code
capacity = 40
passengers = 0
stops = int(input("Enter number of stops: "))
for stop in range(1, stops + 1):
print("Stop", stop)
alighting = int(input("Passengers alighting: "))
boarding = int(input("Passengers boarding: "))
if alighting < 0 or boarding < 0 or alighting > passengers:
print("Invalid passenger counts")
else:
passengers = passengers - alighting + boarding
print("Passengers on bus:", passengers)
if passengers > capacity:
print("Capacity violation!")
else:
print("Within capacity")
